MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_001: Dagsion's getting back to its lively old atmosphere,\ndon't you think?
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_002: Plenty of bad things happened here, but with its\npeople returning, it reminds me of what it used to be.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_003: I agree. I'm very pleased by what I've seen.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_004: I remember when I left Ribeira and saw the imperial\ncapital for the first time. I was so impressed.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_005: You know, my whole world changed the day you\nshowed up in my village.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_006: Indeed it did. Though we had no idea about\neverything that was ahead of us.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_007: That was the day I came to speak with Castor about\nhis impending execution.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_008: You and Pop were the best of friends at one time.\nCan I ask how you got so close?
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_009: Castor was my student when he was a\nvulkan candidate.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_010: After he became a full-fledged vulkan, he and I\nresolved a number of troublesome cases together.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_011: I found that I could easily talk to him. That's rare for\nsomeone like me who's...wound a little tightly.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_012: So when it came time for his execution, I felt like I\nshould be the one to bring him in.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_013: I met you in Ribeira. You made your way back to the\ncapital with Castor, where you reunited with Aurora.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_014: And now here you are, such a wonderful warrior.\nFate is truly stranger than we can imagine.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_015: Back home, I never dreamed my life would go\nthis way.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_016: I want to tell you something that someone in my\nposition should not say.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_017: I'm very glad that you saved Castor. Thank you, Cai.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_018: Don't give it a second thought. I appreciate how you\nprotect my mom, as a vulkan, after all.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_019: And don't worry about what someone in your\n"position" needs to do. Just be yourself.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_020: I'm the impulsive one. It's kinda my thing. And you...\nare perfect the way you are.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_021: That's the kind of thing Castor would say.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_022: Oh yeah? You think maybe I'm like Pop?
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_023: Yes. He had no fear of villains who hid in the\nshadows of law and power. He was relentless.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_024: I'd be conflicted, hesitating, second-guessing every\nmove, but Castor went straight for the neck.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_025: Really? It's so strange to think of Pop that way. But it\ndoes make me happy.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_026: In those days, it felt like my job was to clean up the\nmesses he left in his wake.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_027: And you. You're not so easy either. Entering the\nHeroic Games without a second thought.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_029: Sure. Some stuff might have...happened.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_030: I suppose it falls to me to look out for both mother\nand son now.
MID_SE_Kai_Cen_C_031: And I'm grateful. Just go easy on me, 'K?